Subject: [PATCH] Place sysroot symlinks by each file's repository

_symlink_sysroot_tree strips the repository path from each file using the
target's repository, so a file that a target forwards from another
repository, such as a filegroup in the main repository selecting part of
a toolchain, kept its external/<repo> prefix in the sysroot. rustc_lib's
libraries then weren't in the sysroot's lib directory, where rustc's
RUNPATH looks for them; rustc only found them when its symlink resolved
into the toolchain repository, as it does locally but not on a remote
executor. Each file's own repository is stripped instead.
---

diff --git a/rust/private/toolchain.bzl b/rust/private/toolchain.bzl
--- a/rust/private/toolchain.bzl
+++ b/rust/private/toolchain.bzl
@@ -150,9 +150,13 @@
         # symlink matching this path can be created within the sysroot.
 
         # The code blow attempts to parse any workspace names out of the
-        # path. For local targets, this code is a noop.
-        if target.label.workspace_root:
-            file_path = file.path.split(target.label.workspace_root, 1)[-1]
+        # path. For local targets, this code is a noop. The file's own
+        # repository counts, not the target's: a target may forward files
+        # from another repository, as a filegroup selecting part of a
+        # toolchain does.
+        workspace_root = file.owner.workspace_root if file.owner else target.label.workspace_root
+        if workspace_root:
+            file_path = file.path.split(workspace_root, 1)[-1]
         else:
             file_path = file.path
 
